Nimbus Sans L — copyright notice (INCOMPLETE: licence grant still missing)
==========================================================================

Covers: data/font-nimbussansl.pk3dir/fonts/n019004l.pfb
        data/font-nimbussansl.pk3dir/fonts/n019004l.afm
        data/font-nimbussansl.pk3dir/fonts/n019004l.pfm
Work:   Nimbus Sans L Bold (URW++ Design & Development), Type 1, version 1.06

This is a third-party work redistributed unmodified. It is NOT covered by COPYING.xonotic's
blanket "GPL version 3 or any later version" grant.


The copyright notice, VERBATIM from the font files
---------------------------------------------------

The .pfb carries this in its cleartext header as `/Notice`, and the .afm repeats it as its
`Notice` line. The two agree exactly, which is the cross-check that it was read correctly.
Reproduced with the PostScript `\050` / `\051` escapes resolved to the parentheses they encode:

    Copyright (URW)++,Copyright 1999 by (URW)++ Design & Development;
    Cyrillic glyphs added by Valek Filippov (C) 2001-2002

Supporting metadata from the same headers, for identifying which release this is:

    FontName    NimbusSanL-Bold
    FullName    Nimbus Sans L Bold
    FamilyName  Nimbus Sans L
    Version     1.06
    Generated   by pfaedit, 2002-12-31


What is still missing, and why this file does not guess at it
---------------------------------------------------------------

**The licence grant itself is not present in any file we ship.** Everything above is a copyright
notice — it identifies the rights holder, it does not state the terms under which the work may be
redistributed. Those terms are not in the .pfb, the .afm, or the .pfm; the search that produced
this file looked at every printable run in the binaries' cleartext.

URW++ donated several Nimbus faces to the Ghostscript project, and the family has been
distributed under more than one licence over time — GPL and AFPL for the 1996 Type 1 release,
LPPL for a 2009 release. That history is exactly why this file does not name one: which grant
applies depends on which release this 2002-dated, pfaedit-generated build descends from, and
that cannot be settled from the bytes on disk.

To close this properly, take the licence file as shipped by the upstream package this font came
from — the Ghostscript fonts distribution (`COPYING` alongside the URW fonts) or the Debian
`gsfonts` package copyright file — and add it here. Do not substitute a licence found by
searching for the font's name: several redistributors have relabelled these files.

Until then this notice at least travels with the work, and identifies the rights holder
verbatim, which is strictly better than the nothing that shipped before it.


Provenance of this file
-----------------------

Written 2026-07-30. The quoted notice is a byte-for-byte extraction from the font files in this
repository. Nothing here is transcribed from memory or summarised from a web page; where the
authoritative text is absent, this file says so rather than filling the gap. See
data/licenses/FONTS for the other three font packs.
